    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23(4) Defence service requirement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012#sch-1-sec-23-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In this section:\nmember of the family unit of a person has the same meaning as in\nthe Migration Act 1958.\nPermanent Forces means the Permanent Navy, the Regular Army\nor the Permanent Air Force.\nrelevant defence service: a person has completed relevant defence\nservice if:\n\n(a) the person has undertaken a total of at least 90 days service in\none or more of the Permanent Forces (whether or not that\nservice was continuous); or\n\n(b) the person has undertaken a total of at least 90 days service\non which he or she was required for, and attended and was\nentitled to be paid for, duty in one or more of the Reserves\n(whether or not that service was continuous); or\n\n(c) the person:\n\n(i) was discharged from service undertaken in one of the\nPermanent Forces or the Reserves as medically unfit for\nthat service; and\n\n(ii) became so unfit because of service undertaken in any of\nthe Permanent Forces or the Reserves.\nReserves means the Naval Reserve, the Army Reserve or the Air\nForce Reserve.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00119\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nservice: a person undertakes service in the Permanent Forces or the\nReserves only if the person is appointed, enlisted or transferred\ninto any of the Permanent Forces or the Reserves.\nNote:\nFor appointment, enlistment or transfer into any of the Permanent\nForces or the Reserves, see the Naval Defence Act 1910, the Defence\nAct 1903 and the Air Force Act 1923.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In this section:\nmember of the family unit of a person has the same meaning as in\nthe Migration Act 1958.\nPermanent Forces means the Permanent Navy, the Regular Army\nor the Permanent Air Force.\nrelevant defence service: a person has completed relevant defence\nservice if:\n\n(a) the person has undertaken a total of at least 90 days service in\none or more of the Permanent Forces (whether or not that\nservice was continuous); or\n\n(b) the person has undertaken a total of at least 90 days service\non which he or she was required for, and attended and was\nentitled to be paid for, duty in one or more of the Reserves\n(whether or not that service was continuous); or\n\n(c) the person:\n\n(i) was discharged from service undertaken in one of the\nPermanent Forces or the Reserves as medically unfit for\nthat service; and\n\n(ii) became so unfit because of service undertaken in any of\nthe Permanent Forces or the Reserves.\nReserves means the Naval Reserve, the Army Reserve or the Air\nForce Reserve.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00119\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nservice: a person undertakes service in the Permanent Forces or the\nReserves only if the person is appointed, enlisted or transferred\ninto any of the Permanent Forces or the Reserves.\nNote:\nFor appointment, enlistment or transfer into any of the Permanent\nForces or the Reserves, see the Naval Defence Act 1910, the Defence\nAct 1903 and the Air Force Act 1923.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012-sch-1-sec-23-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cf9afd2b368a0820ded1aea6e00694d58482bae6fe39adef7417cc5c6c841926",
      "skos:note": "A person has completed relevant defence service if they have undertaken a total of at least 90 days service in one or more of the Permanent Forces or the Reserves."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-defence-families-act-2012#sch-1-sec-23-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23(4) Defence service requirement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In this section:\nmember of the family unit of a person has the same meaning as in\nthe Migration Act 1958.\nPermanent Forces means the Permanent Navy, the Regular Army\nor the Permanent Air Force.\nrelevant defence service: a person has completed relevant defence\nservice if:\n\n(a) the person has undertaken a total of at least 90 days service in\none or more of the Permanent Forces (whether or not that\nservice was continuous); or\n\n(b) the person has undertaken a total of at least 90 days service\non which he or she was required for, and attended and was\nentitled to be paid for, duty in one or more of the Reserves\n(whether or not that service was continuous); or\n\n(c) the person:\n\n(i) was discharged from service undertaken in one of the\nPermanent Forces or the Reserves as medically unfit for\nthat service; and\n\n(ii) became so unfit because of service undertaken in any of\nthe Permanent Forces or the Reserves.\nReserves means the Naval Reserve, the Army Reserve or the Air\nForce Reserve.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00119\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nservice: a person undertakes service in the Permanent Forces or the\nReserves only if the person is appointed, enlisted or transferred\ninto any of the Permanent Forces or the Reserves.\nNote:\nFor appointment, enlistment or transfer into any of the Permanent\nForces or the Reserves, see the Naval Defence Act 1910, the Defence\nAct 1903 and the Air Force Act 1923."
    },
    {
